Hi, 

It seems that the behavior of SNANA relative to DLMU computation changes depending on if we use host or no:

Without host, ZHEL seems to be updated such as: 1 + ZHEL = (1 + ZCMB) * (1 + VPEC/C) * (1 + Z_CMB_TO_HEL) and then DL seems to be evaluated as DL = (1 + ZHEL) * (1 + Z_CMB_TO_HEL) * COMOV_DIST(ZCMB)) with VPEC contains in ZHEL.

However when using host, updates of DLMU in sntools_hos (maybe in TRANSFER_SNHOST_REDSHIFT) seems to throw away the velocity from DLMU computation (even when using random vel not provided by the HOSTLIB). 


Since the two ways do not seem completely correct (even if peculiar velocity effect on DLMU is really small) maybe DLMU computation can be a function of VPEC as:

```
double gen_dLmag(double zCMB, double zHEL, double VPEC, double GLON, double GLAT ) {

  // Returns lumi-distance mag with input cosmology
  // Note that INPUTS.H0 ~ 70 km/s/Mpc, and H0 -> ~2E-18

  double mu ;
  if ( zCMB <= 1.0E-10 ) { return 0.0 ; }  // avoid inf, May 2013

  if ( INPUTS.ANISOTROPY_INFO.USE_FLAG ) {
    INPUTS.ANISOTROPY_INFO.GLON = GLON;
    INPUTS.ANISOTROPY_INFO.GLAT = GLAT;
  }

  mu = dLmag (zCMB, zHEL, &INPUTS.HzFUN_INFO, &INPUTS.ANISOTROPY_INFO );

 // add peculiar velocity effect
  mu += 10 * log10(1 + VPEC / LIGHT_km)

  return(mu) ;

} // end of gen_dLmag
```
Where zHEL in this example does not contains VPEC

