In the original BBC code (and paper), the z-range for the biasCor  extends a little past user-input zmax in order to interpolate the biasCor in the latter half of the last z-bin. Somewhere in all the updates and refactors, this biasCor redshift-padding got lost (a bug). If zmax is past the detection of a survey, there is no impact from this bug. However, for running BBC with a limited z-range, the missing redshift padding can result in a large loss of events due to invalid biasCor. 

The fix is in function set_CUTMASK();
 double zmin = INPUTS.zmin ;
 double zmax = INPUTS.zmax ;
  if ( IS_BIASCOR && !INPUTS.restore_bug_zmax_biascor )
    { zmax += SAMPLE_BIASCOR[idsample].BINSIZE_REDSHIFT ; }

and note that input restore_bug_zmax_biascor=1 will restore the bug.

For the foundation test above with 0.01<z<0.03, the missing biasCor fraction is 47% with bug, and 3.4% with fix.

